steps.do:
Map the PIN answer:
- shared it with someone → yes_shared;
- believes it was observed or skimmed → yes_observed;
- says it was not compromised → no;
- unsure → unknown.

Check the four required conditions:
(1) the customer reported within 60 days of the statement date showing the transaction (if the records do not settle this, ask the customer when it first appeared on a statement);
(2) the category is unauthorized_transaction, card_present_fraud, card_not_present_fraud, atm_cash_discrepancy or duplicate_charge;
(3) the customer agreed to a written statement;
(4) the account is OPEN with no holds or restrictions.
If all four hold, credit is required: set provisional_credit_eligible to true. This holds even when a NOT REQUIRED condition also applies: that list says credit 'may be offered at discretion', so true is allowed under both passages.
If any of the four fails, credit is not required: set false. It may still be offered at discretion.
Tell the customer whether provisional credit applies.

Confirm each filed dispute, giving:
- its category;
- whether provisional credit applies: the full amount, reduced by the $50 or $500 liability if reported late, issued within 10 business days (20 for accounts under 30 days old);
- the investigation timeline: 45 business days, or 90 for international, POS outside the US, or new accounts;
- any affidavit due;
- the card action.
Say that if the investigation goes against them, provisional credit is reversed only after at least 3 business days' written notice. Name any dispute not filed, and why.
